TOMBSTONE 01 ~~> THE KNOWN-BAD THAT WAS NEVER FED TO THE MACHINE
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
WHAT IT WAS
  The malformed-door test built a bad i13 move (6 tokens), checked
  i13valid() on it separately, then called engineCycle() — which
  generated its OWN move internally from the payload and passed.
  The bad move was validated in a corner and never fed through the door.
HOW IT DIED
  Run before the page. "malformed door: NOT caught (FAIL)" — the
  engine accepted the cycle because the thing it actually gated was
  not the thing the test built.
THE FIX
  engineCycle now takes the move as a REAL input path: a malformed
  payload produces a malformed move that reaches i13 at the door and
  is refused THERE. The test feeds the bad payload through the front
  door, not past it.
LESSON
  Third time this shape appeared in the record: a check that measures
  a value the machine never saw. A known-bad you describe but never
  feed is not a known-bad — it is a comment. Feed it through the door.
